{
  "_comment": [
    "Fixed rosters for the 2026-fall league (Aug 1 -- Dec 31, 2026).",
    "",
    "Roster fields (per player):",
    "  name     -- CANONICAL display_name (matches Steam scoreboard). Used for",
    "              team inference on ingested screenshots and for individual stats.",
    "  role     -- 'core' | 'support' | 'stand_in'. Mid/carry/offlane are cores.",
    "              league_result.side_team reads a side from its non-stand_in",
    "              players, so this field decides who identifies a team.",
    "  position -- 'mid' | 'carry' | 'offlane' | 'support'. From the captains'",
    "              sheet. Display only; nothing resolves identity from it.",
    "  tier     -- 1-4, or 'legend'. The draft pool the player came from.",
    "              Display only.",
    "  aka      -- friendly nicknames used by !register so players don't have to",
    "              know the canonical Steam name ('Cpx' -> 'Mandark [<MC>]').",
    "              The Teams tab DISPLAYS aka[0] with the canonical underneath.",
    "  backup   -- optional. Canonical name of the stand-in who can substitute",
    "              FOR THIS SLOT, or a LIST of them. On the sheet these are the",
    "              second name in a cell like 'BeetleBum/Soooze'.",
    "",
    "2026-08-14 SEASON RESET. The league was rebuilt from a tier draft and",
    "every recorded result was archived (league_ingest.py --reset-season",
    "2026-fall-v1 -> data/archive/). The 11 games from the first attempt are",
    "in that archive, not in the ledger. data/matches.json was not touched:",
    "the lobby is a different system and a league reset costs it nothing.",
    "",
    "2026-08-19 RESHUFFLE. Team names came from the captains and the whole",
    "sheet moved with them: no_nakhra_clan (1), cpx_king (2), khanna_clan (3),",
    "gillu_&_co (4), axo_clan (5). Seeker went 3->2, Vanzo 2->3, BeastMode",
    "4->3, Bashira 3->4, Oden Jr 5->2, Germ and Tiger-Y off the stand-in",
    "benches and into starting slots on 1 and 2. league_ingest.py",
    "--freeze-teams was run FIRST, so the seven recorded games keep the team",
    "they were played for -- recomputing would have read them as mixes.",
    "",
    "!! TEAM 5 HAS FOUR STARTERS. The sheet's offlane cell says TBD, and",
    "   naming somebody to fill it would be inventing a player. MIN_STARTERS",
    "   is 3, so four starters plus a stand-in still resolves. Fill the cell",
    "   and add them here.",
    "",
    "!! TEAM 6 IS ON THE SHEET AND NOT IN THIS FILE. It lists Narai (mid)",
    "   and Vanilla (carry) with three TBDs, and neither name appears in",
    "   either ledger. A sixth team changes the schedule shape -- six teams",
    "   over two slots means TWO byes a night, not one -- so it waits until",
    "   the roster is real and the captains say so.",
    "",
    "Khuni Billa came off Team 1's starting five and is a stand-in there now.",
    "A name may map to exactly one team, so he stays on that roster.",
    "",
    "STILL UNIDENTIFIED -- no Steam name, so a game they play in cannot be",
    "attached to a series until someone says which scoreboard name is theirs:",
    "  Team 5 'Eros' (carry)",
    "  Team 5 'Eldritch' (support)  stand-ins 'Theekra' and 'Rebel'",
    "Everyone else on the sheet maps to a name already in the ledgers.",
    "",
    "STAND-INS ARE SHARED and are not tied to one team. side_team resolves a",
    "side from its STARTERS and lets registered stand-ins fill the rest,",
    "whichever team's sheet they sit on -- Scarface [FUBU] filled a Team 1",
    "slot and a Team 3 slot on consecutive nights in the first season.",
    "",
    "A NAME MAY MAP TO EXACTLY ONE TEAM. league_result.team_index is a flat",
    "dict, so a second entry wins or loses by iteration order. Shared",
    "stand-ins therefore sit on one roster and appear in other teams'",
    "`backup` lists, which are display-only.",
    "Stand-ins are listed on the roster of whichever team is their home for identity purposes only; every team may field any of them, and the `backup` lists say who covers which slot.",
    "",
    "open_pool: players who registered via `!register` in Discord but aren't",
    "on any team's fixed roster. Captains can pull from the pool for stand-ins.",
    "The pool is written by tools/discord_league.py, never by hand."
  ],
